edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186098935 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186098936 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186098935 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186098937 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186098935 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186098938 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186098935 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186098939 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186098935 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186098940 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186098935 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186098935 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186098935 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186098936 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186098935 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "76405eb1-2f74-542e-aab9-001fe5ee76ff" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186098936 #edb/ref 1080 "\\frac{10}{3}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186098936 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186098936 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "a93b98b3-fc61-5f38-b2cf-0e4d0d84697e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186098937 #edb/ref 1080 "\\frac{7}{3}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186098937 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186098937 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "15bf6613-ed49-5c14-8962-302fba899942" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186098938 #edb/ref 1080 "\\frac{1}{3}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186098938 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186098938 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "2553718f-9dc9-58d5-b044-7b0ec9b75acc" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186098939 #edb/ref 1080 "\\frac{2}{3}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186098939 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186098939 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "6e5c77a9-0ae1-5fca-9298-b1a2fbddfb48" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186098940 #edb/ref 1080 "\\frac{5}{3}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186098940 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186098940 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "70c7b215-8a02-5ef3-8a75-f44389330a1f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186100733 #edb/ref 1069 "e-547" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186100733 #edb/ref 1071 "Find the values of $c$ that satisfy the mean value theorem for integrals for  $f(x) = x^2-2x+2$ on the interval $[0,3].$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186100733 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "a0f21b4c-0f5c-5567-aaec-9da481d2e7ac" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186100733 #edb/ref 1074 "Applying the mean value theorem for integrals, we have\n\n$$\n\\eqalign{\n       f(c) (b-a)  & =  \\int_a^b f(x) \\, \\textrm dx \\[5pt]\n              f(c)    & = \\dfrac {1}{b-a} \\int_a^b f(x) \\, \\textrm dx \\[5pt]\n    & = \\dfrac {1}{3-0} \\int_0^3  (x^2-2x+2) \\, \\textrm dx \\[5pt]\n     & =  \\left . \\dfrac {1}{3} \\cdot  \\left[\\dfrac{x^3}{3} -x^2 +2x\\right] \\right|_0^3 \\[5pt]\n    & =   \\dfrac {1}{3} \\cdot \\left[ \\left(\\dfrac{3^3}{3} -3^2 +2\\cdot3\\right) -  \\left(\\dfrac{0^3}{3} -0^2 +2\\cdot0\\right)\\right] \\[5pt]\n    & =  \\dfrac {1}{3}\\cdot6 \\[5pt]\n    &  = 2.\n}\n$$\n\n    \n\nNow, we use the expression for $f(x)$ to solve for the value of $c\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(c) & =2 \\\\ {c}^{2}-2c+2 & =2 \\\\ c(c-2) & =0 \\\\ c & =0,2.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186100734 #edb/ref 1069 "e-548" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186100734 #edb/ref 1071 "Find the average value of the function $f(x) = x - 2$ on the interval $[-2, 4].$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186100734 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "0c84fc6d-422e-5729-94d2-a12cda71f78d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186100734 #edb/ref 1074 "Applying the average value formula, we find that the average value of the function is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{\\text{avg}} & =\\frac{1}{b-a}\\,{\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4-(-2)}{\\int }_{-2}^{4}x-2\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}(\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}-2x){|}_{-2}^{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}[(\\frac{{4}^{2}}{2}-2(4))-(\\frac{(-2)^{2}}{2}-2(-2))] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}[(8-8)-(2+4)] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}(0-6) \\\\  & =-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186100735 #edb/ref 1069 "e-549" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186100735 #edb/ref 1071 "Find $c$ such that the average value of $g(x) = 3 x$ on the interval $[0,c]$ is equal to $3.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186100735 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "244bb10c-4c6f-5be0-bd9a-72b4defee245" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186100735 #edb/ref 1074 "To solve for $c,$ we apply the average value formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{g}_{\\text{avg}} & =\\frac{1}{b-a}\\,{\\int }_{a}^{b}g(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ 3 & =\\frac{1}{c-0}\\,{\\int }_{0}^{c}3x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ 3 & =\\frac{1}{c}(\\frac{3{x}^{2}}{2}){|}_{0}^{c} \\\\ 3 & =\\frac{1}{c}(\\frac{3{c}^{2}}{2}-0) \\\\ 3 & =\\frac{3c}{2} \\\\ c & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186100736 #edb/ref 1069 "e-550" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186100736 #edb/ref 1071 "The graph of the function $f(x),$ which is defined on $[1,6],$ is shown below. The areas of the regions between the graph and the $x$-axis are $5$ and $2,$ respectively (from left to right). Find the average value of $f(x)$ on $[1,6].$ \n\n![](images/64/6433d1ca57ceb334f304e894e2655ef50d987567fbcf219314302bb381fd9a83.png)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186100736 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "a1572338-79f7-5da7-b9f6-552dcb7984a6" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186100736 #edb/ref 1074 "The average value of a function on a given interval is\n\n$$\nf_\\textrm{avg} = \\dfrac{1}{b-a}\\int_a^b f(x) \\: \\textrm{d}x.\n$$\n\nHere, we see that\n\n$$\n\\int_{1}^{6} f(x)\\: \\textrm{d}x = -5 + 2 = -3.\n$$\n\nSo, applying the average value formula, we find that the average value is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{\\text{avg}} & =\\frac{1}{b-a}{\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6-1}\\cdot (-3) \\\\  & =-\\frac{3}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186101021 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186048187 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186101021 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186050819 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186101021 #edb/ref 103