[17592186101024 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186459287 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186101024 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186459291 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186101024 #edb/ref 1039 "Finding the Average Value of a Function Given a Graph" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186101024 #edb/ref 1041 #edb/ref 17592186100736 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186101024 #edb/ref 1042 #uuid "cd9167b4-572f-589f-9b94-b62ba57eb28f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186101060 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186101908 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186101060 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186101909 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186101060 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186101910 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186101060 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186101911 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186101060 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186101912 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186101060 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186101913 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186101060 #edb/ref 1044 #edb/ref 17592186045463 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186101060 #edb/ref 1045 "The Average Value of a Function" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186101060 #edb/ref 1046 #edb/ref 17592186101908 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186101060 #edb/ref 1049 #edb/ref 17592186049280 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186101060 #edb/ref 1050 1380.0 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186101060 #edb/ref 1050 1380.0 #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186101060 #edb/ref 1053 #uuid "e770d350-fe93-58e5-a551-254f24aea748" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186101269 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186098935 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186101269 #edb/ref 1069 "q-18144" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186101269 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186101269 #edb/ref 1071 "![](images/d6/d661fd02727800f40ccaaf7f388b99b61b9e3a2d6c2da351c47b2166d1182b48.png)\n\nThe graph of the function $f(x)$, which is defined on $[-3,6]$, is shown above. The areas of the regions between the graph and the $x$-axis are $40$, $20$ and $10,$ respectively (from left to right). Find the average value of $f(x)$ on $[-3,6].$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186101269 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "794367ad-cee9-50fc-b4cc-e78beb478cad" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186101269 #edb/ref 1074 "The average value of a function on a given interval is\n\n$$\n{f}_{\\text{avg}}=\\frac{1}{b-a}{\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nHere, we see that\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{-3}^{6}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=40-20+10=30.\n$$\n\nSo, applying the average value formula, we find that the average value is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{\\text{avg}} & =\\frac{1}{b-a}{\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6-(-3)}\\cdot (30) \\\\  & =\\frac{30}{9} \\\\  & =\\frac{10}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186101908 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186101909 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186101908 #edb/ref 1061 618980 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186101908 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "d75b1c61-1292-5625-8252-d8c10bae2e1b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186101908 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186102034 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186101909 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186101910 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186101909 #edb/ref 1061 618981 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186101909 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "3e6aeea7-0134-5101-a19a-c37ab846bb82" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186101909 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186101021 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186101910 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186101911 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186101910 #edb/ref 1061 618984 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186101910 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "42fd3643-e43b-5a23-8553-5171fa424230" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186101910 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186102035 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186101911 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186101912 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186101911 #edb/ref 1061 618985 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186101911 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "89d80bd5-bf3f-5758-a57c-65437a4424dd" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186101911 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186101022 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186101912 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186101913 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186101912 #edb/ref 1061 618989 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186101912 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "3a6cc496-9cd7-5d8a-b41a-b6ed6646b019" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186101912 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186101023 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186101913 #edb/ref 1061 618992 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186101913 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "3d3e3cfa-978d-5956-a57b-742f51ee2e89" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186101913 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186101024 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186102034 #edb/ref 1064 "The region $\\textrm{R},$ shown below, is the area under the graph of $f(x) = 2x+1$ over the interval $[1,3].$ What is the height of the rectangle defined over the same interval that has the same area as $\\textrm{R}?$ \n\n![](images/01/01597200b1f0e147fa8c53b6301d0c8e37208b5a6cce64cf0d9859d1220d8385.png)\n\n \n\nUsing the formula for the area of a trapezoid, we have that\n\n$$\n\\eqalign{\n\\textrm{Area}\\,(\\textrm{R}) = \\dfrac{1}{2}(3+7)(3-1)= 10.}\n$$\n\nFor the rectangle to have the same area, we must have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}10 & =f(c)(3-1) \\\\ f(c) & =5 \\\\ 2c+1 & =5 \\\\ c & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can summarize what we've just done by saying that\n\n$$\n\\int_1^3 (2x +1)\\, \\textrm d x= f(2) \\cdot (3-1).\n$$\n\nThis is an example of the **mean value theorem for integrals**, which states:\n\n*If $f(x)$ is a continuous function on the closed interval $[a, b]$, then there exists a number $c$ in that interval such that*\n\n$$\n\\int_a^b f(x)\\, \\textrm d x = f(c) \\cdot (b-a).\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186102034 #edb/ref 1065 986 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186102034 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "c1b3241c-c8fd-514f-aa8c-a000710896d4" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186102034 #edb/ref 1067 "Introduction" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186102035 #edb/ref 1064 "The **average value** of a continuous function on a closed interval $[a,b]$ is given by\n\n$$\nf_\\textrm{avg} = \\dfrac{1}{b-a}\\int_a^b f(x) \\: \\textrm{d}x.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186102035 #edb/ref 1065 988 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186102035 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "1cced554-b7fa-5fd4-b8b5-86c8e0bb4bc0" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186102035 #edb/ref 1067 "The Average Value of a Function" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186295716 #edb/ref 1080 "\\frac{5}{2}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186295716 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186295716 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "4e2aa02f-a4ec-550a-ade8-9e48bb5f1850" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186295782 #edb/ref 1080 "1,\\,\\frac{5}{2}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186295782 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186295782 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "59648138-a114-51e5-892e-a0c2df92248a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186296359 #edb/ref 1080 "-\\frac{5}{2},\\,1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186296359 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186296359 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "cfe67af0-fcaf-5d5e-a56d-77eb12803f63" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186296381 #edb/ref 1080 "-\\frac{1}{2},\\,5" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186296381 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186296381 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "d38fcd7d-c6b8-55d1-8fad-9a37e56de360" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186296486 #edb/ref 1080 "\\frac{9\\pi -4}{16}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186296486 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186296486 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "e4f22f82-3f4c-56a7-8fca-b1699296b03b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186296629 #edb/ref 1080 "\\frac{1}{2},\\,5" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186296629 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186296629 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "ff2eab6a-2a27-5e35-9dc7-aaca0c578fb1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186296838 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186295716 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186296838 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186295782 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186296838 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186296359 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186296838 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186296381 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186296838 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186296629 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186296838 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186296838 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186296838 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186295782 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186296838 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "6374f584-b639-5c44-b777-84bde5e5310d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186297137 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186296486 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186297137 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045492 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186297137 #edb/ref 1077 "field-1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186297137 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186296486 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186297137 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "f5ebfc2e-32f9-5714-a71a-21c80776c9ec" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186297304 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186296838 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186297304 #edb/ref 1069 "q-30872" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186297304 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186297304 #edb/ref 1071 "Find the numbers $c$ such that the average value of $f(x)=-6{x}^{2}+14x-5$ on the interval $[0,c]$ is equal to $0.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186297304 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "16b1bc24-13e7-5da4-a569-33e3816b732d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186297304 #edb/ref 1074 "To solve for $c,$ we apply the average value formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{\\text{ave}} & =\\frac{1}{b-a}{\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ 0 & =\\frac{1}{c-0}{\\int }_{0}^{c}(-6{x}^{2}+14x-5)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ 0 & ={\\frac{1}{c}(-2{x}^{3}+7{x}^{2}-5x)|}_{0}^{c} \\\\ 0 & =\\frac{1}{c}[(-2{c}^{3}+7{c}^{2}-5c)-0] \\\\ 0 & =-2{c}^{2}+7c-5 \\\\ 2{c}^{2}-7c+5 & =0 \\\\ (c-1)(2c-5) & =0 \\\\ c & =1,\\,\\frac{5}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186297462 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186297137 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186297462 #edb/ref 1069 "q-316309" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186297462 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186297462 #edb/ref 1071 "![](images/1c/1c69b5a43e445861a728fcd8faed9e89b3bcb61141ad35d99e60f2a43983244d.png)\n\nThe graph of the function $f(x),$ which is defined on $[-2,9],$ is shown above. It consists of three line segments and the arc of the semi-circle centered at $(5,0)$ with radius $3.$ \n\nFind the average value ${f}_{\\text{avg}}$ of $f(x)$ on $[0,8].$ Do not round the answer.\n\n${f}_{\\text{avg}}=$\n{{field-1}}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186297462 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "4e5a2c9b-15eb-580e-9b48-bc6a0c515d66" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186297462 #edb/ref 1074 "The average value of a function on a given interval $[a,b]$ is \n\n$$\n{f}_{\\text{avg}}=\\frac{1}{b-a}{\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nUsing the additive property of the definite integral, we write\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{0}^{8}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x={{{\\int }_{0}^{2}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x}_{⏟}}_{-{A}_{1}}+{{{\\int }_{2}^{8}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x}_{⏟}}_{{A}_{2}}.\n$$\n\nThe 1st integral represents the signed area between the curve and the $x$-axis, where $x\\in [0,2].$ The corresponding region is a right triangle, so we find the area using the formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{1} & =\\frac{1}{2}bh \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 2\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the region lies below the $x$-axis, we have \n\n$$\n{\\int }_{0}^{2}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=-{A}_{1}=-2.\n$$\n\nThe 2nd integral represents the signed area between the curve and the $x$-axis, where $x\\in [2,8].$ The corresponding region is a semi-circle, so we find the area using the formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{2} & =\\frac{1}{2}\\pi {r}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\pi \\cdot {3}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{9\\pi }{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{8}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =-{A}_{1}+{A}_{2} \\\\  & =-2+\\frac{9\\pi }{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, using the formula for the average value, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{\\text{avg}} & =\\frac{1}{b-a}{\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{8-0}\\cdot (-2+\\frac{9\\pi }{2}) \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{4}+\\frac{9\\pi }{16} \\\\  & =\\frac{-4+9\\pi }{16} \\\\  & =\\frac{9\\pi -4}{16}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186302781 #edb/ref 1080 "0" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186302781 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186302781 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "34272274-e39f-56d1-b23d-d6f2a622e4a6" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186302796 #edb/ref 1080 "{56.5}^{∘}F" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186302796 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186302796 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "36d4f785-6f5a-5ce0-bf69-39aad915511d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186302890 #edb/ref 1080 "{52.1}^{∘}F" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186302890 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186302890 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "45450f39-4901-5335-a3d0-7f1c044bd30e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186302923 #edb/ref 1080 "{61.2}^{∘}F" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186302923 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186302923 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "4a1d0fe5-2d24-59ed-9880-fe68d2d0d545" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186302948 #edb/ref 1080 "\\frac{\\pi }{2}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186302948 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186302948 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "4e6335c6-35ae-5399-8646-8a48ae96cd75" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186302984 #edb/ref 1080 "{50.0}^{∘}F" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186302984 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186302984 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "559548da-50f2-521b-9452-7fc3e2890a87" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186303198 #edb/ref 1080 "{58.9}^{∘}F" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186303198 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 175921860454