7] [17592186304464 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186304464 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186304464 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186303198 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186304464 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "8fac5b99-d1c6-5e15-afc2-0e7b3ba2570b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186304792 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186304464 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186304792 #edb/ref 1069 "q-3289" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186304792 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186304792 #edb/ref 1071 "During the winter in Pasadena, the temperature, in ${F}^{∘}$, $t$ hours after $9$ a.m. can be modeled by the function $T(t)=50+14\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi t}{12}).$ Find the average temperature during the period from $9$ a.m. to $9$ p.m." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186304792 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "2e55b4cb-6c56-5cac-893d-482f84ce6bec" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186304792 #edb/ref 1074 "Since the function is valid starting from $9$ A.M., we can conclude our interval is $[0,12].$\n\nApplying the average value formula, we find that the average value of the function is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{T}_{\\text{avg}} & =\\frac{1}{b-a}{\\int }_{a}^{b}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{12-0}{\\int }_{0}^{12}(50+14\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi t}{12}))\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\frac{1}{12}(50t-\\frac{168}{\\pi }\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi t}{12}))|}_{0}^{12} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{12}[(50\\cdot 12-\\frac{168}{\\pi }\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi \\cdot 12}{12}))-(50\\cdot 0-\\frac{168}{\\pi }\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi \\cdot 0}{12}))] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{12}[(600-\\frac{168}{\\pi }\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\pi ))-(0-\\frac{168}{\\pi }\\operatorname{cos}⁡(0))] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{12}[(600-\\frac{168}{\\pi }\\cdot (-1))-(-\\frac{168}{\\pi }\\cdot 1)] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{12}[\\frac{600\\pi +168}{\\pi }+\\frac{168}{\\pi }] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{12}(\\frac{600\\pi +336}{\\pi }) \\\\  & =\\frac{600\\pi +336}{12\\pi } \\\\  & ≈{58.9}^{∘}F.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186304800 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186304085 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186304800 #edb/ref 1069 "q-3297" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186304800 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186304800 #edb/ref 1071 "Within  the interval $[0,\\pi ]$, determine the average value of $f(x)=2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186304800 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "24f38454-bd1c-55d7-83bd-a807c36fe3b4" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186304800 #edb/ref 1074 "Applying the average value formula, we find that the average value of the function is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{\\text{avg}} & =\\frac{1}{b-a}{\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\pi -0}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }(2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }(2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\frac{1}{\\pi }(-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x)|}_{0}^{\\pi } \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\pi }[(-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\pi )+\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\cdot \\pi ))-(-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(0)+\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\cdot 0))] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\pi }[(-2\\cdot (-1)+\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 1)-(-2\\cdot 1+\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 1)] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\pi }[(\\frac{5}{2})-(-\\frac{3}{2})] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\pi }(4) \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{\\pi }.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186428159 #edb/ref 1030 0.5 #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186428159 #edb/ref 1032 "Initial Codex estimate from captured target-band crossing frequency. Selected account foundations: 1 rises / 2 eligible passed source activities = 0.500000; nearest selected fraction = 1/2. Crossing activity numbers [1]; waits [1]. Separate account estimates: foundations=1/2 (1/2). Selection: most observations, then lower weight, then account name; no averaging. Singl